   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Impact Shake\n\nHeavy content slams down from above with a squash, a damped camera jolt, a two-frame RGB split and dust puffs kicking out sideways. The built-in subject is a big word; a host puts its own content in by replacing the .is-word elements.\n\nCategory: camera. Length: 1.667 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A launch word, a price or a logo should land like it weighs a ton.\n- A hype edit or a social teaser needs one hard-hitting beat on the drop.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The landing only needs a light accent around a small element: use trim-burst.\n- The element should fly in sideways with motion streaks: use speed-lines.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"LAUNCH\"\n- intensity (number, 0-2): Intensity, default 1\n- impact (number, 1-20): Impact frame, default 7\n- background_color (color): Background, default \"#111111\"\n- foreground_color (color): Foreground, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- split_a_color (color): Split A, default \"#FF2A2A\"\n- split_b_color (color): Split B, default \"#2A6BFF\"\n- dust_color (color): Dust, default \"#D9D9D9\"\n- seed (number, 1-99): Seed, default 1\n- speed (number, 0.25-3): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
